  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:102714",
  "description": "Ruby is the interpreted scripting language for quick and easy object-oriented programming. It has many features to process text files and to do system management tasks (as in Perl). It is simple, straight-forward, and extensible.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-93577)\n  * ruby: integer overflow issue in CI/CD regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-97229)\n  * ruby: integer overflow issue in regular expression compiler (CVE-2026-110264)\n  * ruby: ruby: Heap-based buffer overflow via string case conversion (CVE-2026-132825)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * ruby4.0: Rebase to the latest Ruby 4.0 release [rhel-10] (JIRA:RHEL-260673)\n  * ruby4.0: Rebase to the latest Ruby 4.0 release [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:RHEL-312591)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
